imestamp":"2026-11-12T07:09:37.582Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"43ad64df-9fa2-4f03-b09b-d717d94c69da","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0a3077be-f3d6-44b7-a169-c1486d08c4f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vizo9Qd5um7HzhZ2SmrtMW","type":"tool_result","content":"- [ERN formal exploratory passes](ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md) — French briefs, MM-02/MM-03/MM-23/J3/derivability, Spec 2 m1–m3 (WC2–WC4), m4 handoff (WC5, corpus v4–v6, ChainExcl, PlaceExcl), m4 event pass (WC5.1, corpus v8, po/sw/hb), m4 herd7/RC11 litmus pass, m4 strict mutex edge (corpus v9), m4 layer E event fragment (WC5.1 corrigé), m4 layer R mutex realization (corpus v10, 3 controller counterexamples) and corrective pass (Run6, proposed C22.4/C18 amendments, W-NC), reports/ never merged, spec in ~/Downloads, axiom rule\n- [No Co-Authored-By trailer](feedback-no-coauthored-by.md) — never add the Claude co-author line to commits; main rewritten 2026-11-05\n      46 ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md\n- Spec 2 jalon 3, complétude et corpus (2026-11-09): branch `formal/spec2-m3` from `e30355f`, brief `~/Downloads/brief-spec2-m3.md`, corpus `~/Downloads/corpus-spec2-m3.md` (verdicts come from it, never from the model), WC4 file named `ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC4.md` in the brief is `~/Downloads/ERN_WC4.md` on disk. Library state is `SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg`; `Encap` unchanged, read on `(st.1, st.2.1)`; arena ops `NewArenaPreC`/`IssueStepC`/`ResetStepC` in `SyncLib.lean` (issue = split then store via `opStepC`, i.e. store re-indexed on `ancestorC`; literal `IssueD` on the view rejects corpus S3 step 8, witness `S3_8_view_literal`). Unified §56 guard needs invariant `AdminSep` (cross-registry), required by T4 only for issue/reset (conditional hypothesis keeps the m1 statement). New modules `ArenaPreserve`, `ArenaConservativity`, `RealizeSound`, `Corpus/{MX,AR,Frames,S10,Witness}`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m3.md` (part B = consolidated index m1–m3). Open findings: S10 corpus `reject` vs model `ok` (§63.7 silent on frame-held authorities whose anchor moves), S11 setup needs a ceded observe derivative for C14.3. Proof tips: give `(E := …)` explicitly in `IssueStepC.ok` and define states with `s.A.length` (not literals) or `decide` unification times out; `akeep_of_A (s := …) (s' := …)` converts view/flat `AKeep`; `FramesC (s.set t)` needs `framesC_set`, not defeq. Review (4 parallel read-only agents, one per lens, then one targeted re-check) found W-C22.2 \"never enabled again\" refuted by an ordinary `release` (`W_C22_2_reenable`). Never auto-fix report line numbers by script: in `a, b (:N)` lists the number belongs to the last name; re-check each fix by opening the line.\n- Spec 2 jalon 3 clôture (2026-11-10): same branch `formal/spec2-m3`, corpus v3, report `formal/reports/spec2-m3-close.md`; owner kept the three extra theorems (`S10_2_ok`, `S10_3_ok`, `W_C22_2_cycle`). Corpus v4 then aligned S11 setup and W-C22.2 on the P7 criterion.\n- Spec 2 jalon 4 passe 1, passation (2026-11-10): branch `formal/spec2-m4` from `b4d18ce`, candidate `~/Downloads/ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC5.md` (C43–C46 L1/L2, OB-C17/18), corpus `~/Downloads/corpus-spec2-m3.md` v4. Modules `Cap`, `Encap5`, `CapPreserve`, `Corpus/{GuardedRead,CapValues,Encap5Witness,GuardedChain,S10b,L1Evidence}`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-handoff.md`. Findings: L1 false for `cap` (W-GR acquire); `cap5_sound` and `handoff_loss_exists` false because `GuardedExcl` only checks the access argument while §43 is recursive along holder chains (z stored in T, exercised via guarded); `cap5_compat` proved (`attr_compat`); L1 `cap5_drop_own : DDSound k → Cap5DropOwn k L` proved for all 28 labels (2026-11-11; `CapPreserve` + `CapDrop`, transport restricted to authorities with some effective mode, exit/endUse/free via post-state `NoDangling`, spawnVal via `create_yield`/`yield_transfers` and `KBase`). GuardedExcl/CtlExcl play no role in L1 or state-form L2; `cap5` under-reports exercise (chains through guarded), so OB-C17 not discharged for real accesses. `auth_compat` duplicates `effective_exclusive`, `footprint_ne` duplicates `exists_mem_footprint` (disclosed, not refactored). Sequential helpers worth reusing: `EndFree.OnlyReleases`, `Frames.exitG_*`, `EndFree.chain_root_unique`, `rootHeldConv_active`, `TransferPreserveAux.transfer_base`. Test of the GuardedExcl fix (2026-11-11, `Encap5C.lean`, `Corpus/GuardedChainC.lean`): `Exer5` = ExercisableAt from the current frame with no live guarded on the holder chain, `ChainExcl` requires it for derive/split/read/write/writeShared, `Encap5C ⊆ Encap5`; `cap5_sound_C` and `handoff_loss_exists_C` proved; the locked variant of the counterexample is admitted and its marker is c1's unlock (`lc_handoff_marker`); mutex-free steps always satisfy ChainExcl. ChainExcl is my proposition, not WC5's: adoption is the owner's call. Extension to rights over places (2026-11-11, brief + corpus v6 §2 sexies W-GS, `Encap5R.lean`, `Corpus/{GuardedStore,PlaceExclWitness}.lean`, commits `960fb94`..`475e297`): `HasRight5` (HasRight with Exer5), `PlaceExcl k L st` (needs arena reg, layout, contract), `Encap5R ⊆ Encap5C`; W-GS step 1 (owner `store` into T without lock via guarded held by slot, partial sharing `o := derive(root_M, Observe, {lock})`) is admitted by Encap5C and excluded by PlaceExcl; twin, lc_trace, S2(=cycle_trace5), S3 to issue, S4, S10 admitted. `placeExcl_of_noLive` needs WC5 C21.6 RegBound (spawnVal creation phase can revive a dormant entry). Open choices reported: alloc disjunction mirrored with Exer5 on §68 branch; absent objects → True (MetaRight vs ResetD). Uncovered: Grounds clauses (§63.4, §69.2, §70.3), issue dst premises, newMutex C13.2, resetLock C18.1 (Exer5 impossible: arg is the live guarded), unlock, newArena.\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, event pass (2026-11-11): same branch `formal/spec2-m4`, candidate `~/Downloads/ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC5.1.md` (replaces WC5), corpus v8 (§2 septies: hb facts for W-HO/W-HO′/W-HO″ and twins W-HO-J, W-HO″-J, lc_trace); owner accepted écarts 10–13 of the PlaceExcl pass. Modules `Events` (Run5R, Steps5R explicit-state runs, `Ev` step/start keyed by spawn position at 2i/2i+1, PO/SW/HB = TransGen, `reachList` one-pass decision so `decide` works on hb, ExclPair, Race, `lossStep` via `find?`, HandoffOrderedAt existential), `EventsCompose` (`lossStep_own`, `handoffOrdered_no_race` under exactly the hypotheses of `handoff_loss_exists_C`), `EventsProtocols` (`spawn_orders`, `join_orders`, `lock_orders` with hb-hypothesis form + holder corollary), `Corpus/HandoffEvents`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-events.md`, commits `3a5699a`..`7700b0d`, 1726 theorems (1225 non-internal). `lossStep_own` is not a corollary of `handoff_loss_exists_C` (its drop step need not cross the compat threshold). WC5.1 C4 only says identities are fresh; `|C|` is the model (`spawnEff`). Cite only clauses actually opened this session.\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, herd pass (2026-11-11): same branch, `formal/herd/` (13 C litmus tests, `run.sh`, raw `results/`, README in English), report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-herd.md`, commits `3b5e7ce`..`c4c5d15`. herd7 7.58 is at `~/.opam/default/bin/herd7` (not on PATH); pass `-model rc11.cat` (C default is `c11_partialSC.cat`), `-skipcheck <name>` skips a check, races show as `Undef` / `Flag *undef*`. herd's C dialect rejects `&local` in CAS (use a shared pointer); `*x` is non-atomic whatever the type. The three-thread lock test takes ~6.5 min. The brief's exclusivity condition (\"never both r0 = 0\") is met by legal successive acquisitions; overlap shows only by skipping `atomicity` and `coherencermw` (plus `SC` for seq_cst). Complement (same day, commits `5c27f9b`..`8ab315d`): group D `XCHG+{acq,rlx,sc}` (my B7 renamed to `XCHG+acq`), group E `RS+rel+rlx` (rc11 `rs` includes a later same-thread non-RMW atomic write; WC5.1 C48 keeps the C++20 form, so that program races there; owner wants the term \"écriture atomique non-RMW\"), and the skip-check runs are in `run.sh` with outputs `results/<test>+skip-<checks>.txt`. In zsh, `$a` holding several options is not word-split: use `${=a}` or literal arguments.\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, strict mutex edge (2026-11-11): corpus v9 §2 octies (prefix P, W-RL₀, W-RL, W-RL-J, W-TR, W-TR-J), modules `EventsStrict` (`ctlAt`, `MutexGap`, `SWS` copied from `SW`, `HBS`, `RaceS`, `HandoffOrderedS`, inclusion lemmas), `EventsStrictProtocols` (`*S` versions, `lock_ordersS_gaps` finer form), `RegIndex` (`reg_stable`: registry never shortens, guarded kept per index), `Corpus/{MutexEdge,MutexEdgeStrict}`; section added to `formal/reports/spec2-m4-events.md`; commits `358ce63`..`fa4d3ec`, 1801 theorems (1275 non-internal). Encap5R admits `resetLock` unchecked (no conjunct constrains it; C22.6 exception = OB-C28). WC5.1 C13 only says \"registers\"; append/in-place is the model. This project has autoImplicit on: an unopened name in a statement becomes a variable (caught only because `decide` failed).\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, tranche 2, layer E (2026-11-11): `~/Downloads/ERN_WC5_1_FINAL.md` = « WC5.1 corrigé », replaces WC5.1 for citations; the three strict-edge decisions accepted. Autonomous event fragment in `formal/Ern/Concurrency/EventModel/` (`Closure`: generic TransGen decision by table rounds + counting, no edge-order assumption; `Graph`: init = event 0, po = listing order, rf/mo as pair lists, `EventConsistent` = 5 named conjuncts; `Lemmas`; `Witness` G1–G19), all with `set_option autoImplicit false`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-eventmodel.md`; commits `978ce1d`..; 1956 theorems (1348 non-internal). Results: all G1–G19 as expected; G12 (two unsynchronized RMWs reading init) passes coherence `hb;eco?`, only conjunct 3 rejects it (no `coherencermw` analogue); G18 has a race in the fragment vs none under rc11 (release sequences).\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, tranche 2, layer R (2026-11-12): corpus v10 §2 nonies (declared realization of the reference mutex, W-RC, controller-graph facts); 7 hypotheses of the brief. Modules `EventModel/Complements` (G1 backward, `hb_trans`, `hb_closure`, `eco_irrefl` under conjuncts 1–3 via an mo-rank measure), `Corpus/ResetLockRight` (W-RC: step 4 resetLock `ok` without any right on lock), `MutexReal/{Graph,Coherence,Classify,ClassifyWitness,Bridge,Witness}`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-mutexreal.md`; commits `4b719a3`..`83b6adf`; 2295 theorems (1521 non-internal). Graph: init = newMutex(e), events filterMap of acquire/unlock/resetLock on registry index e, mo = index order, rf (j, j+1) per RMW; invariant and coherence need only LStep + no taken grant initially (no Encap5R); bridge needs no hyp 3, converse needs `CtlFixed` (W-TR refutes it otherwise). Classification found 3 counterexamples admitted by Encap5R (store(z, lock), alloc(owner = lock), issue(..., lock2)): C22.4 only covers read3/write3/writeShared. Review lesson: an empty footprint \"by definition\" (free/exit/terminate) is a blocking pattern; add the dying leaves and prove via `SyncInv.control` after the step (`lstep_preserves`). Cite Spec 1 only after reading `specs/` (Lean comments' § numbers are not evidence).\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, layer R corrective pass (2026-11-12): proposed amendments `~/Downloads/ERN_WC5_2_amendements_proposes.md` (C22 item 4 replacement, C18 item 4) tested, not validated; corpus v11 §2 decies; owner accepted `Touches` and the `release(guarded)` observation. Modules `MutexReal/{Amend,AmendWitness,NonRegression,Classify6,Classify6Witness,ResetAmend}`, `Corpus/NewMutexRight`; commits `866849f`..`c394671`; 2397 theorems (1592 non-internal). `TouchesX` = Touches + depend's `result` place itself; `CtlRestr` reads the post-state (dead-after exception), C22.3 exception literal (`TransferExcl`/`EncapVals`); `Run6`, `RunAm` (resetLock + `CtrlRight`). Results: 3 counterexamples refused, twins and all Run5R traces (+ W-GS twin, S3, S10 restated) are Run6; spawnVal under hyp 3 proved via the short route (source leaf → `Moved`, contradicts `ctlInit`); completeness without kind restriction proved; depend clause has no necessity witness; W-NC step 3 (`newMutex` from a frame without right on lock) is ok; `Run6` over-restricts `alloc(owner = M)` (leaf-level Touches). Count lesson: lazily realized equation lemmas (`Label.termOf.eq_1`) get re-attributed to a later module that also realizes them; count new theorems by name set difference against a saved baseline dump.\n- Spec files live in `~/Downloads/` (`ERN_Memory_model.md` = v0.2 incl. MM-03.1/03.2, `ERN_Memory_Model_v0.3_consolidee.md`, `ERN_Memory_Model_0.3.3.md` = MM-03.3 v0.2), not in `specs/`.\n\n**Why:** the briefs require French commit messages (one per step), docstrings citing `MM-0x.y` rules, statement changes justified in the report, and say `formal/reports/` is exploration never merged into `main`. Later briefs add \"arbitrages\" that answer earlier report questions.\n\n**How to apply:** start a new pass from the latest branch tip; run an adversarial review workflow over module and report before delivering; `lake` is not on PATH, call `~/.elan/bin/lake`; keep the Lake library name `Ern`. `formal/Ern/.gitkeep` keeps showing as deleted: restore it with `git checkout`, never commit the deletion. A post-commit hook can make `git commit` exceed 2 minutes: give it a long timeout. The axiom rule ({propext, Quot.sound} only) forbids core lemmas that pull `Classical.choice` (`List.getElem?_mapIdx`, `List.eq_nil_iff_forall_not_mem`, `List.nodup_range`, `List.pairwise_lt_range`): sweep `#print axioms` over every theorem and replace them with local lemmas. Mathlib tactics (`set`, `tauto`) are unavailable. Reviews keep catching report errors: quote old forms from the old commit, count declarations with a command, and base an evidence claim only on a check that would fail on the defect. After fixing review findings, run a second targeted review of the fixes: in MM-03 pass 2 a fix over-rejected legitimate programs. Before calling a clause \"missing\" from an arbitrage, re-read every earlier arbitrage still in force: in pass 3 the clause needed for exitFrame_no_dangling was A4's root-holder rule, which A1 puts in WF3 and pass 2 had left out. `timeout` does not exist on this Mac: run `lake build` directly (about 2.5 min). When an arbitrage enlarges a definition used in hypotheses (pass 4: `Inv3` gained `NoDangling`), theorems whose text is unchanged silently narrow: give them only the conjunct they use. Before retiring a counterexample whose witness breaks a new invariant clause, look for another witness: pass-4 review found one and flagged the weakening as major. Check obligations against the initial state: the base frame of `S3.init` owns no place, so an obligation about it can be vacuous on reached states. A review fix can itself pick a semantic reading (pass 5: the kind conjunct of `IsInternalFor` rejected a `newArena` that D3 leaves undecided): check every fix for verdicts it changes on cases the text is silent on. Module docstrings must cite the report's own numbering, not the review's decision numbers. Arbiter-supplied theorems can be false: check them on small reached states (owned storage, a parameter that is the ancestor of another) before trying a proof. Every factual claim in the report needs a module witness, or reviewers flag it; never say \"blocked until X\" without checking escape sequences such as ending the owner value. When a precondition gains clauses, lemmas taking it as a hypothesis narrow silently: name the old precondition (pass 7: `EnterPreBase`) and give the lemmas only what they use. A guard on one operation (G2 on `store`) is usually bypassable through another (a helper authority then `release`/`endUse`/`free`/exit): look for such bypasses before claiming a configuration is excluded. A new check on an operation with a defined failure (`issue` → `fail`) must not turn that failure into `reject`. Use one adversarial reviewer per arbitrage lens; each found distinct real issues in pass 7. When a restriction rejects an old counterexample, try to rebuild a witness that satisfies the new clause before restating it as a rejection (pass 8: a same-shape destination restored `transfer_not_inv3_preserving`). Drop hypotheses a proof does not use. When cases disappear because their state is no longer reached, replay their verdicts on a new reachable state and list the drops. Machine-check every changed verdict the report lists, including the old witnesses' rejected steps. Never state \"only clause X fails\" as `X → Pre` next to `¬ X`: that is vacuous; name the other clauses (pass 8: `TransferPreBase` with an iff) and state them. Run a second targeted check after fixing verification findings: in pass 8 it caught that vacuous form. `omega` proving a conjunction goal pulls `Classical.choice`: split the goal first; `omega` closing a non-arithmetic goal (e.g. `∃ l, …` from contradictory hypotheses) does too: write `exact absurd h (by omega)`. `meta` is a keyword in this Lean: never name a hypothesis `meta`. `set` (Mathlib) is unavailable: use `obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ : ∃ x, x = e := ⟨_, rfl⟩`. `if_pos`/`if_neg`/`ite_cond_eq_true` are deprecated: use `simp only [h, ↓reduceIte]`. When `S3.Usable.mono` is applied with `rfl` for `hP`, give `(s := …) (s' := …)` explicitly or it unifies the wrong way. Simulation theorems: never quantify obligations over all translations (vacuous); put them as per-step premises of the run with parameters fixed once, and give a concrete multi-step run as witness. A universal encoding obligation (`∀ addr, decode (enc addr) = addr`) is unsatisfiable by a finite computable decode: state it per value. `lake env lean` uses the last built olean: rebuild the module before a scratch file uses new declarations. Never use an unquoted heredoc for Lean or docstrings: backticks run as shell commands; use `<<'EOF'` and pass paths by environment variable. `example`s escape a `collectAxioms` sweep: rename them to theorems in a scratch copy to check their axioms. `awk length` counts bytes, not characters: count line length in Python. Each check round finds errors in the previous round's wording: when a sentence is fixed in a docstring, grep the report for the same claim; quote arbitrages exactly (L2 said \"hypothèse des énoncés\", not \"hors langage\"); classify every item a deliverable asks to classify instead of moving it aside; a summary must not present a hypothesis restated in a conclusion as a result. Count theorem constants with internal ones (`isInternal`) and say which count you give. A callee cannot move a value out of a parameter's footprint (`ActiveDerivedOutside` counts the parameter itself): build values to transfer as callee locals. Authority ids shift with every alloc/issue/split: check them with `#eval` of `prun` prefixes before writing a case. A literal invariant from the material can fail under the full kernel extension: keep the literal statement with counterexamples and prove the parts that hold, under their own names. A runner's fallback state must be unreachable (e.g. no frame) or a statement \"the run's state is reached\" is vacuous when the run fails; give a lemma deriving success from reachability. Projecting `.2` out of an existential passes the elaborator but fails in the kernel: use `obtain`. When `step_ok_of`-style lemmas time out at `whnf`, pass the contract `k` and statics explicitly. Jalon 3 took four check rounds (11/9/9/4 confirmed): each round's fixes need their own narrow check. The list `Sublist` notation `<+` is scoped: write `List.Sublist`; `List.take_add` pulls `Classical.choice`. `omit … in` goes before the docstring. A `def` in a `variable (k : K)` section takes `k` only if it uses it: check call sites. In a multi-line `{ st with … }`, put each field on its own line at one column. Theorems stated for registered arenas (`ar ∈ s.arenas`) do not carry over to library instances: never cite them for one. Before writing \"the only effect of X is Y\", look for a witness in the other direction (derivability: the missing guard also turned a `fail` into an `ok`).\n- Spec 1 v0.1 validated and frozen by the owner on 2026-11-06: file stays `specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md` (project convention: version in the file name; an unversioned rename in 3f9fee2 was reverted by 9b33c26 on 2026-11-07); v0 file deleted, owner tags `memory-model-v0` on main. PR ernlang/ern#2 ready for review, not merged. Inter-spec boundaries: KExt (§42), §86 typing → Spec 4, MM3-H H16 → Spec 3, MM23-H16 → Spec 8 (address) + Spec 11 (width/encoding); the lowest-address rule is a non-normative reference realization, not §82.3. Next-revision note: §81 omits Spec 8. Owner rule: Lean comments carry no decision history (dates, validations, restatements).\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ecc41b7b-cf34-4af5-bc33-252bdefa06a0","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:09:38.198Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"- [ERN formal exploratory passes](ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md) — French briefs, MM-02/MM-03/MM-23/J3/derivability, Spec 2 m1–m3 (WC2–WC4), m4 handoff (WC5, corpus v4–v6, ChainExcl, PlaceExcl), m4 event pass (WC5.1, corpus v8, po/sw/hb), m4 herd7/RC11 litmus pass, m4 strict mutex edge (corpus v9), m4 layer E event fragment (WC5.1 corrigé), m4 layer R mutex realization (corpus v10, 3 controller counterexamples) and corrective pass (Run6, proposed C22.4/C18 amendments, W-NC), reports/ never merged, spec in ~/Downloads, axiom rule\n- [No Co-Authored-By trailer](feedback-no-coauthored-by.md) — never add the Claude co-author line to commits; main rewritten 2026-11-05\n      46 ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md\n- Spec 2 jalon 3, complétude et corpus (2026-11-09): branch `formal/spec2-m3` from `e30355f`, brief `~/Downloads/brief-spec2-m3.md`, corpus `~/Downloads/corpus-spec2-m3.md` (verdicts come from it, never from the model), WC4 file named `ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC4.md` in the brief is `~/Downloads/ERN_WC4.md` on disk. Library state is `SC × SyncReg × ArenaReg`; `Encap` unchanged, read on `(st.1, st.2.1)`; arena ops `NewArenaPreC`/`IssueStepC`/`ResetStepC` in `SyncLib.lean` (issue = split then store via `opStepC`, i.e. store re-indexed on `ancestorC`; literal `IssueD` on the view rejects corpus S3 step 8, witness `S3_8_view_literal`). Unified §56 guard needs invariant `AdminSep` (cross-registry), required by T4 only for issue/reset (conditional hypothesis keeps the m1 statement). New modules `ArenaPreserve`, `ArenaConservativity`, `RealizeSound`, `Corpus/{MX,AR,Frames,S10,Witness}`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m3.md` (part B = consolidated index m1–m3). Open findings: S10 corpus `reject` vs model `ok` (§63.7 silent on frame-held authorities whose anchor moves), S11 setup needs a ceded observe derivative for C14.3. Proof tips: give `(E := …)` explicitly in `IssueStepC.ok` and define states with `s.A.length` (not literals) or `decide` unification times out; `akeep_of_A (s := …) (s' := …)` converts view/flat `AKeep`; `FramesC (s.set t)` needs `framesC_set`, not defeq. Review (4 parallel read-only agents, one per lens, then one targeted re-check) found W-C22.2 \"never enabled again\" refuted by an ordinary `release` (`W_C22_2_reenable`). Never auto-fix report line numbers by script: in `a, b (:N)` lists the number belongs to the last name; re-check each fix by opening the line.\n- Spec 2 jalon 3 clôture (2026-11-10): same branch `formal/spec2-m3`, corpus v3, report `formal/reports/spec2-m3-close.md`; owner kept the three extra theorems (`S10_2_ok`, `S10_3_ok`, `W_C22_2_cycle`). Corpus v4 then aligned S11 setup and W-C22.2 on the P7 criterion.\n- Spec 2 jalon 4 passe 1, passation (2026-11-10): branch `formal/spec2-m4` from `b4d18ce`, candidate `~/Downloads/ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC5.md` (C43–C46 L1/L2, OB-C17/18), corpus `~/Downloads/corpus-spec2-m3.md` v4. Modules `Cap`, `Encap5`, `CapPreserve`, `Corpus/{GuardedRead,CapValues,Encap5Witness,GuardedChain,S10b,L1Evidence}`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-handoff.md`. Findings: L1 false for `cap` (W-GR acquire); `cap5_sound` and `handoff_loss_exists` false because `GuardedExcl` only checks the access argument while §43 is recursive along holder chains (z stored in T, exercised via guarded); `cap5_compat` proved (`attr_compat`); L1 `cap5_drop_own : DDSound k → Cap5DropOwn k L` proved for all 28 labels (2026-11-11; `CapPreserve` + `CapDrop`, transport restricted to authorities with some effective mode, exit/endUse/free via post-state `NoDangling`, spawnVal via `create_yield`/`yield_transfers` and `KBase`). GuardedExcl/CtlExcl play no role in L1 or state-form L2; `cap5` under-reports exercise (chains through guarded), so OB-C17 not discharged for real accesses. `auth_compat` duplicates `effective_exclusive`, `footprint_ne` duplicates `exists_mem_footprint` (disclosed, not refactored). Sequential helpers worth reusing: `EndFree.OnlyReleases`, `Frames.exitG_*`, `EndFree.chain_root_unique`, `rootHeldConv_active`, `TransferPreserveAux.transfer_base`. Test of the GuardedExcl fix (2026-11-11, `Encap5C.lean`, `Corpus/GuardedChainC.lean`): `Exer5` = ExercisableAt from the current frame with no live guarded on the holder chain, `ChainExcl` requires it for derive/split/read/write/writeShared, `Encap5C ⊆ Encap5`; `cap5_sound_C` and `handoff_loss_exists_C` proved; the locked variant of the counterexample is admitted and its marker is c1's unlock (`lc_handoff_marker`); mutex-free steps always satisfy ChainExcl. ChainExcl is my proposition, not WC5's: adoption is the owner's call. Extension to rights over places (2026-11-11, brief + corpus v6 §2 sexies W-GS, `Encap5R.lean`, `Corpus/{GuardedStore,PlaceExclWitness}.lean`, commits `960fb94`..`475e297`): `HasRight5` (HasRight with Exer5), `PlaceExcl k L st` (needs arena reg, layout, contract), `Encap5R ⊆ Encap5C`; W-GS step 1 (owner `store` into T without lock via guarded held by slot, partial sharing `o := derive(root_M, Observe, {lock})`) is admitted by Encap5C and excluded by PlaceExcl; twin, lc_trace, S2(=cycle_trace5), S3 to issue, S4, S10 admitted. `placeExcl_of_noLive` needs WC5 C21.6 RegBound (spawnVal creation phase can revive a dormant entry). Open choices reported: alloc disjunction mirrored with Exer5 on §68 branch; absent objects → True (MetaRight vs ResetD). Uncovered: Grounds clauses (§63.4, §69.2, §70.3), issue dst premises, newMutex C13.2, resetLock C18.1 (Exer5 impossible: arg is the live guarded), unlock, newArena.\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, event pass (2026-11-11): same branch `formal/spec2-m4`, candidate `~/Downloads/ERN_Concurrency_Model_WC5.1.md` (replaces WC5), corpus v8 (§2 septies: hb facts for W-HO/W-HO′/W-HO″ and twins W-HO-J, W-HO″-J, lc_trace); owner accepted écarts 10–13 of the PlaceExcl pass. Modules `Events` (Run5R, Steps5R explicit-state runs, `Ev` step/start keyed by spawn position at 2i/2i+1, PO/SW/HB = TransGen, `reachList` one-pass decision so `decide` works on hb, ExclPair, Race, `lossStep` via `find?`, HandoffOrderedAt existential), `EventsCompose` (`lossStep_own`, `handoffOrdered_no_race` under exactly the hypotheses of `handoff_loss_exists_C`), `EventsProtocols` (`spawn_orders`, `join_orders`, `lock_orders` with hb-hypothesis form + holder corollary), `Corpus/HandoffEvents`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-events.md`, commits `3a5699a`..`7700b0d`, 1726 theorems (1225 non-internal). `lossStep_own` is not a corollary of `handoff_loss_exists_C` (its drop step need not cross the compat threshold). WC5.1 C4 only says identities are fresh; `|C|` is the model (`spawnEff`). Cite only clauses actually opened this session.\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, herd pass (2026-11-11): same branch, `formal/herd/` (13 C litmus tests, `run.sh`, raw `results/`, README in English), report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-herd.md`, commits `3b5e7ce`..`c4c5d15`. herd7 7.58 is at `~/.opam/default/bin/herd7` (not on PATH); pass `-model rc11.cat` (C default is `c11_partialSC.cat`), `-skipcheck <name>` skips a check, races show as `Undef` / `Flag *undef*`. herd's C dialect rejects `&local` in CAS (use a shared pointer); `*x` is non-atomic whatever the type. The three-thread lock test takes ~6.5 min. The brief's exclusivity condition (\"never both r0 = 0\") is met by legal successive acquisitions; overlap shows only by skipping `atomicity` and `coherencermw` (plus `SC` for seq_cst). Complement (same day, commits `5c27f9b`..`8ab315d`): group D `XCHG+{acq,rlx,sc}` (my B7 renamed to `XCHG+acq`), group E `RS+rel+rlx` (rc11 `rs` includes a later same-thread non-RMW atomic write; WC5.1 C48 keeps the C++20 form, so that program races there; owner wants the term \"écriture atomique non-RMW\"), and the skip-check runs are in `run.sh` with outputs `results/<test>+skip-<checks>.txt`. In zsh, `$a` holding several options is not word-split: use `${=a}` or literal arguments.\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, strict mutex edge (2026-11-11): corpus v9 §2 octies (prefix P, W-RL₀, W-RL, W-RL-J, W-TR, W-TR-J), modules `EventsStrict` (`ctlAt`, `MutexGap`, `SWS` copied from `SW`, `HBS`, `RaceS`, `HandoffOrderedS`, inclusion lemmas), `EventsStrictProtocols` (`*S` versions, `lock_ordersS_gaps` finer form), `RegIndex` (`reg_stable`: registry never shortens, guarded kept per index), `Corpus/{MutexEdge,MutexEdgeStrict}`; section added to `formal/reports/spec2-m4-events.md`; commits `358ce63`..`fa4d3ec`, 1801 theorems (1275 non-internal). Encap5R admits `resetLock` unchecked (no conjunct constrains it; C22.6 exception = OB-C28). WC5.1 C13 only says \"registers\"; append/in-place is the model. This project has autoImplicit on: an unopened name in a statement becomes a variable (caught only because `decide` failed).\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, tranche 2, layer E (2026-11-11): `~/Downloads/ERN_WC5_1_FINAL.md` = « WC5.1 corrigé », replaces WC5.1 for citations; the three strict-edge decisions accepted. Autonomous event fragment in `formal/Ern/Concurrency/EventModel/` (`Closure`: generic TransGen decision by table rounds + counting, no edge-order assumption; `Graph`: init = event 0, po = listing order, rf/mo as pair lists, `EventConsistent` = 5 named conjuncts; `Lemmas`; `Witness` G1–G19), all with `set_option autoImplicit false`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-eventmodel.md`; commits `978ce1d`..; 1956 theorems (1348 non-internal). Results: all G1–G19 as expected; G12 (two unsynchronized RMWs reading init) passes coherence `hb;eco?`, only conjunct 3 rejects it (no `coherencermw` analogue); G18 has a race in the fragment vs none under rc11 (release sequences).\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, tranche 2, layer R (2026-11-12): corpus v10 §2 nonies (declared realization of the reference mutex, W-RC, controller-graph facts); 7 hypotheses of the brief. Modules `EventModel/Complements` (G1 backward, `hb_trans`, `hb_closure`, `eco_irrefl` under conjuncts 1–3 via an mo-rank measure), `Corpus/ResetLockRight` (W-RC: step 4 resetLock `ok` without any right on lock), `MutexReal/{Graph,Coherence,Classify,ClassifyWitness,Bridge,Witness}`; report `formal/reports/spec2-m4-mutexreal.md`; commits `4b719a3`..`83b6adf`; 2295 theorems (1521 non-internal). Graph: init = newMutex(e), events filterMap of acquire/unlock/resetLock on registry index e, mo = index order, rf (j, j+1) per RMW; invariant and coherence need only LStep + no taken grant initially (no Encap5R); bridge needs no hyp 3, converse needs `CtlFixed` (W-TR refutes it otherwise). Classification found 3 counterexamples admitted by Encap5R (store(z, lock), alloc(owner = lock), issue(..., lock2)): C22.4 only covers read3/write3/writeShared. Review lesson: an empty footprint \"by definition\" (free/exit/terminate) is a blocking pattern; add the dying leaves and prove via `SyncInv.control` after the step (`lstep_preserves`). Cite Spec 1 only after reading `specs/` (Lean comments' § numbers are not evidence).\n- Spec 2 jalon 4, layer R corrective pass (2026-11-12): proposed amendments `~/Downloads/ERN_WC5_2_amendements_proposes.md` (C22 item 4 replacement, C18 item 4) tested, not validated; corpus v11 §2 decies; owner accepted `Touches` and the `release(guarded)` observation. Modules `MutexReal/{Amend,AmendWitness,NonRegression,Classify6,Classify6Witness,ResetAmend}`, `Corpus/NewMutexRight`; commits `866849f`..`c394671`; 2397 theorems (1592 non-internal). `TouchesX` = Touches + depend's `result` place itself; `CtlRestr` reads the post-state (dead-after exception), C22.3 exception literal (`TransferExcl`/`EncapVals`); `Run6`, `RunAm` (resetLock + `CtrlRight`). Results: 3 counterexamples refused, twins and all Run5R traces (+ W-GS twin, S3, S10 restated) are Run6; spawnVal under hyp 3 proved via the short route (source leaf → `Moved`, contradicts `ctlInit`); completeness without kind restriction proved; depend clause has no necessity witness; W-NC step 3 (`newMutex` from a frame without right on lock) is ok; `Run6` over-restricts `alloc(owner = M)` (leaf-level Touches). Count lesson: lazily realized equation lemmas (`Label.termOf.eq_1`) get re-attributed to a later module that also realizes them; count new theorems by name set difference against a saved baseline dump.\n- Spec files live in `~/Downloads/` (`ERN_Memory_model.md` = v0.2 incl. MM-03.1/03.2, `ERN_Memory_Model_v0.3_consolidee.md`, `ERN_Memory_Model_0.3.3.md` = MM-03.3 v0.2), not in `specs/`.\n\n**Why:** the briefs require French commit messages (one per step), docstrings citing `MM-0x.y` rules, statement changes justified in the report, and say `formal/reports/` is exploration never merged into `main`. Later briefs add \"arbitrages\" that answer earlier report questions.\n\n**How to apply:** start a new pass from the latest branch tip; run an adversarial review workflow over module and report before delivering; `lake` is not on PATH, call `~/.elan/bin/lake`; keep the Lake library name `Ern`. `formal/Ern/.gitkeep` keeps showing as deleted: restore it with `git checkout`, never commit the deletion. A post-commit hook can make `git commit` exceed 2 minutes: give it a long timeout. The axiom rule ({propext, Quot.sound} only) forbids core lemmas that pull `Classical.choice` (`List.getElem?_mapIdx`, `List.eq_nil_iff_forall_not_mem`, `List.nodup_range`, `List.pairwise_lt_range`): sweep `#print axioms` over every theorem and replace them with local lemmas. Mathlib tactics (`set`, `tauto`) are unavailable. Reviews keep catching report errors: quote old forms from the old commit, count declarations with a command, and base an evidence claim only on a check that would fail on the defect. After fixing review findings, run a second targeted review of the fixes: in MM-03 pass 2 a fix over-rejected legitimate programs. Before calling a clause \"missing\" from an arbitrage, re-read every earlier arbitrage still in force: in pass 3 the clause needed for exitFrame_no_dangling was A4's root-holder rule, which A1 puts in WF3 and pass 2 had left out. `timeout` does not exist on this Mac: run `lake build` directly (about 2.5 min). When an arbitrage enlarges a definition used in hypotheses (pass 4: `Inv3` gained `NoDangling`), theorems whose text is unchanged silently narrow: give them only the conjunct they use. Before retiring a counterexample whose witness breaks a new invariant clause, look for another witness: pass-4 review found one and flagged the weakening as major. Check obligations against the initial state: the base frame of `S3.init` owns no place, so an obligation about it can be vacuous on reached states. A review fix can itself pick a semantic reading (pass 5: the kind conjunct of `IsInternalFor` rejected a `newArena` that D3 leaves undecided): check every fix for verdicts it changes on cases the text is silent on. Module docstrings must cite the report's own numbering, not the review's decision numbers. Arbiter-supplied theorems can be false: check them on small reached states (owned storage, a parameter that is the ancestor of another) before trying a proof. Every factual claim in the report needs a module witness, or reviewers flag it; never say \"blocked until X\" without checking escape sequences such as ending the owner value. When a precondition gains clauses, lemmas taking it as a hypothesis narrow silently: name the old precondition (pass 7: `EnterPreBase`) and give the lemmas only what they use. A guard on one operation (G2 on `store`) is usually bypassable through another (a helper authority then `release`/`endUse`/`free`/exit): look for such bypasses before claiming a configuration is excluded. A new check on an operation with a defined failure (`issue` → `fail`) must not turn that failure into `reject`. Use one adversarial reviewer per arbitrage lens; each found distinct real issues in pass 7. When a restriction rejects an old counterexample, try to rebuild a witness that satisfies the new clause before restating it as a rejection (pass 8: a same-shape destination restored `transfer_not_inv3_preserving`). Drop hypotheses a proof does not use. When cases disappear because their state is no longer reached, replay their verdicts on a new reachable state and list the drops. Machine-check every changed verdict the report lists, including the old witnesses' rejected steps. Never state \"only clause X fails\" as `X → Pre` next to `¬ X`: that is vacuous; name the other clauses (pass 8: `TransferPreBase` with an iff) and state them. Run a second targeted check after fixing verification findings: in pass 8 it caught that vacuous form. `omega` proving a conjunction goal pulls `Classical.choice`: split the goal first; `omega` closing a non-arithmetic goal (e.g. `∃ l, …` from contradictory hypotheses) does too: write `exact absurd h (by omega)`. `meta` is a keyword in this Lean: never name a hypothesis `meta`. `set` (Mathlib) is unavailable: use `obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ : ∃ x, x = e := ⟨_, rfl⟩`. `if_pos`/`if_neg`/`ite_cond_eq_true` are deprecated: use `simp only [h, ↓reduceIte]`. When `S3.Usable.mono` is applied with `rfl` for `hP`, give `(s := …) (s' := …)` explicitly or it unifies the wrong way. Simulation theorems: never quantify obligations over all translations (vacuous); put them as per-step premises of the run with parameters fixed once, and give a concrete multi-step run as witness. A universal encoding obligation (`∀ addr, decode (enc addr) = addr`) is unsatisfiable by a finite computable decode: state it per value. `lake env lean` uses the last built olean: rebuild the module before a scratch file uses new declarations. Never use an unquoted heredoc for Lean or docstrings: backticks run as shell commands; use `<<'EOF'` and pass paths by environment variable. `example`s escape a `collectAxioms` sweep: rename them to theorems in a scratch copy to check their axioms. `awk length` counts bytes, not characters: count line length in Python. Each check round finds errors in the previous round's wording: when a sentence is fixed in a docstring, grep the report for the same claim; quote arbitrages exactly (L2 said \"hypothèse des énoncés\", not \"hors langage\"); classify every item a deliverable asks to classify instead of moving it aside; a summary must not present a hypothesis restated in a conclusion as a result. Count theorem constants with internal ones (`isInternal`) and say which count you give. A callee cannot move a value out of a parameter's footprint (`ActiveDerivedOutside` counts the parameter itself): build values to transfer as callee locals. Authority ids shift with every alloc/issue/split: check them with `#eval` of `prun` prefixes before writing a case. A literal invariant from the material can fail under the full kernel extension: keep the literal statement with counterexamples and prove the parts that hold, under their own names. A runner's fallback state must be unreachable (e.g. no frame) or a statement \"the run's state is reached\" is vacuous when the run fails; give a lemma deriving success from reachability. Projecting `.2` out of an existential passes the elaborator but fails in the kernel: use `obtain`. When `step_ok_of`-style lemmas time out at `whnf`, pass the contract `k` and statics explicitly. Jalon 3 took four check rounds (11/9/9/4 confirmed): each round's fixes need their own narrow check. The list `Sublist` notation `<+` is scoped: write `List.Sublist`; `List.take_add` pulls `Classical.choice`. `omit … in` goes before the docstring. A `def` in a `variable (k : K)` section takes `k` only if it uses it: check call sites. In a multi-line `{ st with … }`, put each field on its own line at one column. Theorems stated for registered arenas (`ar ∈ s.arenas`) do not carry over to library instances: never cite them for one. Before writing \"the only effect of X is Y\", look for a witness in the other direction (derivability: the missing guard also turned a `fail` into an `ok`).\n- Spec 1 v0.1 validated and frozen by the owner on 2026-11-06: file stays `specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md` (project convention: version in the file name; an unversioned rename in 3f9fee2 was reverted by 9b33c26 on 2026-11-07); v0 file deleted, owner tags `memory-model-v0` on main. PR ernlang/ern#2 ready for review, not merged. Inter-spec boundaries: KExt (§42), §86 typing → Spec 4, MM3-H H16 → Spec 3, MM23-H16 → Spec 8 (address) + Spec 11 (width/encoding); the lowest-address rule is a non-normative reference realization, not §82.3. Next-revision note: §81 omits Spec 8. Owner rule: Lean comments carry no decision history (dates, validations, restatements).","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6a90518b-0291-47c5-8795-e5f588da5875","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility