ver share it in requests to external services without asking and getting explicit approval from the user first.\n# gitStatus\nThis is the git status at the start of the conversation. Note that this status is a snapshot in time, and will not update during the conversation.\n\nCurrent branch: formal/spec2-m4\n\nMain branch (you will usually use this for PRs): main\n\nGit user: Guy Senpai\n\nStatus:\n(clean)\n\nRecent commits:\n5148c22 docs(concurrency): complete the final-pass report: clauses read, newMutex steps of Traces, the gap against the tested restriction, line numbers\nb7fa471 test(concurrency): add the newMutex steps of the WC4 traces in Traces to the check of the proposed C13 item 11\n1e9f83c docs(concurrency): state the O10.2 point of the final pass as an unchecked observation\n4372dba docs(concurrency): report the final pass of layer R: final footprint, Run7, amended newMutex, witnesses, non-regression, classification, authority, corollaries and audit\n3913c44 feat(concurrency): state that the amended newMutex keeps the effect and the controller graph, and restate the invariant, coherence and bridge on a final amended execution\n\nClaude Code attached this context automatically; it isn't part of the user's message. It describes the user's own account and workspace, so they don't need it reported back.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
