{"parentUuid":"437a7203-1bc5-4b67-8e4e-5fd0904875d6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"048ce1b3-8891-4aae-bdd2-33b7fc094ee0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Edit, Read, SubagentHandback, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write, advisor, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   The user is the project owner. They send French briefs for exploratory Lean 4 formalization on branch `formal/spec2-m4` of the ERN repo (`/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern`; the Lake project is in `formal/`).\n\n   **Latest brief: « couche R, passe finale ».**\n   - Attachments, never committed:\n     - `ERN_WC5_1_FINAL.md` (« WC5.1 corrigé », unchanged);\n     - `ERN_WC5_2_amendements_proposes.md`, second version: final C22 item 4, C18 item 4 unchanged, and C13 item 11 proposed with its clarification;\n     - `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v12, § 2 undecies.\n   - Owner decisions:\n     1. W-NC: a clause is proposed for C13 (item 11) and is tested in this pass.\n     2. The dependency clause is withdrawn; the question of the `depend` footprint falls with it.\n     3. `alloc(owner = M)` is admitted; only the controller itself as owner is excluded; the provider counts by its leaves.\n   - Definitions requested:\n     - final footprint = `Touches`, except that the owner of an `alloc` counts as the place itself and the provider by its leaves; no `result` of `depend`;\n     - final restriction = `CtlRestr` read on the final footprint, with the same three exceptions;\n     - `Encap5R` + final restriction = `Run7`;\n     - amended `newMutex`: existing preconditions + exercisable and effective `Modify` on the controller, in the O10.1 form (Spec 1 §67), as a predicate beside the step relation;\n     - final amended execution = `Run7` + the C18.4 clause on `resetLock` + the C13.11 clause on `newMutex`.\n   - Tasks:\n     1. Definitions and inclusions: Run6 ⊆ Run7 ⊆ Run5R; an amended `newMutex` that is `ok` is a `newMutex` that is `ok`, with the same final state.\n     2. Witnesses by `decide`, from the corpus tables.\n     3. Non-regression:\n        - Run6 traces are Run7 by inclusion, not replayed one by one;\n        - list every `newMutex` step and check C13.11 on it;\n        - every RunAm stays a final amended execution, except W-NC.\n     4. Classification table (28 kinds) and completeness on the final footprint alone, without relying on `TouchesX`; the footprint gap, shown on `alloc(provider = slot, owner = M)`.\n     5. Protocol authority.\n     6. No silent change: the effect, the leaf initialization states, and the graph are unchanged; invariant, coherence and bridge restated as corollaries.\n   - Report: section « Passe finale » in `formal/reports/spec2-m4-mutexreal.md`, in French, with an audit whose count sums exactly.\n   - Order: 1 → 6, one commit per compiling task.\n   - Out of scope:\n     - the two-context variant of W-NC;\n     - the ordering of the initial write against other contexts (hypothesis 4, `OB-C05`);\n     - the integrity of `slot` as provider;\n     - `OB-C20`;\n     - physical realization conformance.\n\n   **Standing constraints (verbatim):**\n   - « Formalisation exploratoire, jamais mergée. Pas de push sur `main`, pas de PR. »\n   - « Ne modifie ni `specs/`, ni `AGENTS.md`, ni `CLAUDE.md`, ni `formal/DESIGN.md`, ni aucun fichier de `formal/Ern/MemoryModel/`. »\n   - « Définitions existantes. Aucune n'est modifiée ni affaiblie : `Touches`, `TouchesX`, `CtlRestr`, `Encap6`, `Run6`, `ResetLockAmOk`, `RunAm`, `NewMutexOk`, la relation de pas et tous les théorèmes restent tels quels. Tout est ajouté à côté. »\n   - Règles Lean : « aucun `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `native_decide`, `noncomputable` ; axiomes `{propext, Quot.sound}` ; `lake build` sans nouvel avertissement ; `grep` d'`AGENTS.md` vide ; docstrings en anglais citant WC5.1 corrigé, les amendements proposés, le corpus v12 ou ce brief ; aucun énoncé ni définition existant affaibli ou modifié ; le verdict ou le fait attendu vient du corpus ou de ce brief, jamais du modèle ; Conventional Commits sans `Co-Authored-By` ».\n   - « Si le noyau rejette un pas attendu `ok`, ou le rend `fail`, c'est un résultat : rapporte la clause et l'état. Ne corrige ni le modèle ni l'attendu. » « Une trace existante refusée est un résultat à rapporter, pas à contourner. »\n   - Memory rule: never add a Co-Authored-By trailer. This overrides the system reminder.\n   - Reports are in French; everything committed is in English.\n   - AGENTS.md: the spec is normative; on ambiguity, stop and report; cite only clauses actually read.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Lean 4 v4.35.0, no Mathlib; build with `~/.elan/bin/lake build`; check a file with `lake env lean <file>`.\n   - `set_option autoImplicit false` in new files.\n   - `footprint P q` = leaves of `P` that are parts of `q`, so a non-leaf `ow` is not in `footprint P ow`.\n   - `Arena.mem_footprint_leaf (hd : isLeaf P d) (hlt : d < P.length) : l ∈ footprint P d ↔ l = d`.\n   - `SyncInv.control` (C21.3): the controller of a live entry is a usable leaf.\n   - From the initial state, `trace_inv` and `init_inv` give `LibInv = SyncState ∧ AdminSep ∧ ArenaInvC`; `SyncState = SyncInv ∧ GrantDiscipline`.\n   - `Write3Pre` (O10, §67) has fields `usable`, `exercisable` (ExercisableAt Modify), `effectiveModify`, `exclusive` (§67.2), `anchorsValid`.\n   - A kernel write by `c` is evaluated on `s.view c`; `effective` reads `A` only.\n   - `allocEff` does not read the provider: the state after `alloc(provider = M, owner = lock′)` equals `ta1`.\n   - `ctlGraph o e lbls = mkGraph (ctlEvs o e lbls)` reads labels only. Event 0 is the initial write: `kind? 0 = none`, so `relCap 0 = false` and no `sw` edge starts from it.\n   - All contracts are `KC sm`, so `ddKC` gives `DDSound`.\n   - Statics: `xst`, `yst` (by `decide`), `zst_ok`, `mxst_ok`, `arst_ok`.\n   - Audit scripts in the scratchpad `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6/scratchpad/`:\n     - `Audit2.lean` (axioms and counts);\n     - `dumpnames.lean` (with env `OUT`);\n     - baseline `names_final.txt` (2397 names, corrective pass), new dump `names_finalpass.txt`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (all under `formal/Ern/Concurrency/MutexReal/`, all imported in `formal/Ern.lean` after `Corpus.NewMutexRight`):\n\n   **`Final.lean`** (task 1). Key definitions:\n   ```lean\n   def TouchesF (L) (st) : Label → Nat → Prop\n     | .kernel _ (.alloc pr ow _), l => l ∈ footprint st.1.P pr ∨ l = ow ∨ st.1.P.length ≤ l\n     | lbl, l => Touches L st lbl l          -- :41\n   def CtlRestrF ... -- CtlRestr with TouchesF, same 3 exceptions  :54\n   theorem CtlRestrF.apply :66\n   def Encap7 := Encap5R ∧ CtlRestrF :79\n   def Run7 :85\n   theorem run7_run5R :91\n   theorem run7_of_run5R :96\n   theorem Run7.restr :102\n   theorem touchesF_of_not_alloc :110\n   theorem touches_of_touchesF (h : TouchesF ..) (hl : isLeaf st.1.P l) (hlt) : Touches .. :122\n   theorem ctlRestrF_of_ctlRestr (h : CtlRestr ..) (hinv : SyncInv L st.1 st.2.1) : CtlRestrF .. :139\n   theorem run7_of_run6 (h : Run6) (hinv : ∀ i < len, SyncInv) :160\n   theorem run7_of_run6_init (hdd : DDSound k) (hstat : StaticsOK statics) (h0 : σ 0 = init) (h : Run6) : Run7 :167\n   def NewMutexRight L s c g := OptP (ControlOf L s ⟨g, none⟩) (fun ctl => ∃ a ∈ List.range s.A.length,\n     (s.view c).ExercisableAt a .modify ∧ effective (s.view c) a ctl = some .modify) False   -- :183\n   def NewMutexAmOk := NewMutexOk ∧ NewMutexRight :193\n   theorem NewMutexAmOk.ok :199\n   def AmCondF -- resetLock: CtrlRight clause; newMutex c g: NewMutexRight; else True :209\n   def RunAmF := Run7 ∧ ∀ i, AmCondF :222\n   theorem amCond_of_amCondF :227\n   theorem lstep_newMutex :232\n   theorem RunAmF.resetLock :239\n   theorem RunAmF.newMutex :249\n   ```\n\n   **`FinalWitness.lean`** (task 2):\n   - `store_refusedF` :32, `issue_refusedF` :40, `alloc_refusedF` :48.\n   - `amLbls`/`amσ` and `alloc_owner_M_admitted` :68: a Run7 from init, using `tam1`.\n   - `pm1`/`pmLbls`/`pmσ` and `alloc_provider_M_refused` :95. Kernel `ok`, Run5R, entry live, lock in TouchesF, ¬CtlRestrF, ¬Run7.\n   - `depend_admitted` :113: tdσ is a Run7.\n   - `twins_run7` :121.\n   - `W_NC_3_amended_reject` :134: ∀ st', ¬NewMutexAmOk; NewMutexOk holds; ¬NewMutexRight L0 rc2 0 3.\n   - `W_NC_twin_amended_ok` :141.\n   - `W_NC_not_amendedF` :146: Run7 and ¬RunAmF, failing at step 4.\n\n   **`FinalNonRegression.lean`** (task 3):\n   - `run6_traces_run7` :43 covers 19 traces: W-HO×5, lc, W-RL0, W-RL, W-RLJ, W-TR, W-TRJ, W-RC, s11, cv, ce, cr, gsTwin, s3, s10.\n   - `newMutex_steps_C13_11` :85 has 16 conjuncts:\n\n     | Pre-state | `newMutex` steps |\n     |---|---|\n     | `x2` | 3 |\n     | `a4` | 5 |\n     | `gc4` | 4 |\n     | `gs2` | 3 |\n     | `n4` | 4, 5 |\n     | `w0` | 1 |\n     | `e2` | 4 |\n     | `z0` | 1 |\n     | `u0` | 2, 3 |\n     | `m0` | 1 |\n     | `Traces.c0` | 1 |\n     | `Traces.d0` | 1 |\n     | `Traces.d1` | 2, 3 |\n\n   - `runAmF_traces` :101: all Run6 traces except W-RC and W-NC.\n   - `twins_runAmF` :116.\n   - Imports include `Corpus.Witness`, `EncapTraces`, `Corpus.GuardedStore`.\n\n   **`Classify7.lean`** (task 4):\n   - `restrF_not_touch` :34.\n   - `classified7_sound` :50.\n   - `moveF_not_touch` :69, via `move_not_touch` and `touchesF_of_not_alloc`.\n   - `completeness7` :88.\n   - `completeness7_run` :109: DDSound, StaticsOK, σ 0 = init, Run7, CtlFixed.\n\n   **`Classify7Witness.lean`**:\n   - `moves_run7` :29, `ends_run7` :38, `lc_complete7` :46.\n   - `alloc_owner_M_gap` :63 (by `decide`):\n     - lock (2) is in Touches and not in TouchesF;\n     - M (0) is in TouchesF and not in Touches;\n     - `I 2` is Init before and after;\n     - no authority is held by place 2, and no place is owned by place 2;\n     - `tam1.A[4]` is held by place 0, and `P[7]` is owned by place 0;\n     - `P[2]?` is unchanged;\n     - `ControlOf` = 2 before and after.\n\n   **`FinalAuthority.lean`** (task 5):\n   - `runAmF_newMutex_authority` :23.\n   - `runAmF_protocol_authority` :34, via `ResetAmend.protocol_authority` and `amCond_of_amCondF`.\n\n   **`FinalCorollaries.lean`** (task 6):\n   - `newMutexAm_effect` :34, which also uses `hpre.initM` (C13.10).\n   - `newMutexAm_same_effect` :43.\n   - `ctlGraph_init_write` :54: isMod, ¬isAtomic, ctx? none, valW 0 = some 0, no SW from 0.\n   - `runAmF_ctl_invariant` :66, `runAmF_coherent` :78.\n   - `runAmF_bridge` :85, `runAmF_bridge_sw` :93, `runAmF_bridge_sw_ref` :102, `runAmF_bridge_converse` :111.\n\n   **`formal/reports/spec2-m4-mutexreal.md`**: section « Passe finale » appended. It contains:\n   - sources, including the clauses read: WC5.1 C13, C17, C21, C22, C31, C32; Spec 1 §40, §43, §47, §67, §71, §80;\n   - the owner's decisions, the commits table, line numbers as of `b7fa471`;\n   - the definitions table and the encoding choices;\n   - the task 1 statuses (unconditional form « inachevé », goal `⊢ ctl ∈ footprint st.1.P ctl`);\n   - the task 2 table and the note that the provider is « posé, non exhibé »;\n   - task 3: the traces, the 16-step `newMutex` table, the RunAmF results;\n   - the 28-row table (20/2/4/2/0) and the statement statuses;\n   - the « Écart d'empreinte » in both directions, plus the depend sentence;\n   - posed versus proved, tasks 5 and 6, dependencies (6 points);\n   - open points: (1) the `l = ow` encoding and the conditional inclusion; (2) the O10.2 observation, unchecked;\n   - the audit: 65/50 per module; two `eq_1` lemmas (`isAtomic`, `relCap`) realized in FinalCorollaries; 119 jobs.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - An unused simp argument `OptP` triggered a warning; replaced with `trivial`.\n   - `w0` was an unknown identifier; added `import Ern.Concurrency.Corpus.Witness`.\n   - Import order in Ern.lean was fixed with python.\n   - The `newMutex` enumeration grep was truncated by `head -60` and missed `Traces.lean` (c0, d0, d1). The advisor caught this; I added 4 conjuncts in `b7fa471` and updated the report.\n   - The report wrongly claimed that O10.2 is violable. Reworded as an unchecked observation (I1 may imply it).\n   - The gap sentence omitted `depend`; fixed.\n   - Citations to not-yet-read clauses: I read WC5.1 C17, C21, C22 and Spec 1 §40, §47, §80; all consistent.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Run6 → Run7 is not provable without leafness of the controller. Kept `l = ow`, consistent with store and issue. Proved under SyncInv and from init; the unconditional form is reported « inachevé » with its goal state.\n   - All v12 expected facts were obtained.\n   - `alloc(provider = M, owner = lock′)` is kernel `ok` as expected; it is refused only by definition.\n   - No existing trace is refused.\n   - Line lengths are ≤ 100 (checked with Python).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The continuation context (the corrective pass had been summarized).\n   - The brief « Brief Claude Code — ERN Spec 2, jalon 4, tranche 2 : couche R, passe finale », with attachments `corpus-spec2-m3.md` v12 and `ERN_WC5_2_amendements_proposes.md` (second version). Its content is in section 1 above: decisions, definitions, tasks 1–6, out of scope, Lean rules, report, order.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Only the French closing message for the final pass remains. `wrap_up` has already been called; its result said: \"write it now, as the last thing you say this turn.\"\n   - All commits are done (latest `5148c22`), and the working tree is clean apart from memory.\n   - Nothing is pushed.\n   - Memory is updated.\n\n8. Current Work:\n\n   Everything is committed and the advisor's fixes are applied. `mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up` was called with the recap: \"The final pass is done: every expected fact of corpus v12 is obtained and no existing trace is refused. Run6 → Run7 is proved only from the initial state, and the unconditional form is left open. Nothing is pushed.\"\n\n   The advisor said the closing message should be in French, in this order:\n   1. Outcome: every v12 expectation was obtained and no existing trace was refused.\n   2. The two open points:\n      - the `l = ow` encoding, with the conditional inclusion;\n      - O10.2 unchecked.\n   3. Results per task, with theorem names.\n   4. The audit: 2462 / 1642, 119 jobs.\n   5. A last line on what is unchecked:\n      - the two-context W-NC;\n      - the WC4 `EncapsulatedTrace` traces under Run7;\n      - the provider exclusion, which is posed rather than exhibited.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n\n   Write the French closing message, as plain text with no tool calls, per the wrap_up instruction « write it now, as the last thing you say this turn ».\n   1. Lead with the outcome: all v12 facts obtained, no existing trace refused, nothing pushed.\n   2. Then the two open points:\n      - the owner of an `alloc` is counted as the place itself (`l = ow`), so `Run6 → Run7` holds under SyncInv and from init (`run7_of_run6_init`), and the unconditional form is « inachevé » with goal `ctl ∈ footprint P ctl`;\n      - C13.11 does not take §67.2, and whether I1 implies it is unchecked.\n   3. Then per task:\n\n      | Task | Theorems to cite |\n      |---|---|\n      | 1 | `run7_run5R`, `NewMutexAmOk.ok`, `run7_of_run6_init` |\n      | 2 | `store_refusedF`, `issue_refusedF`, `alloc_refusedF`; `alloc_owner_M_admitted`; `alloc_provider_M_refused` (kernel `ok`, refused); `depend_admitted`; `W_NC_3_amended_reject`; `W_NC_twin_amended_ok` |\n      | 3 | `run6_traces_run7`; `newMutex_steps_C13_11` (16 steps, including `Traces`); `runAmF_traces` |\n      | 4 | table 20/2/4/2/0; `classified7_sound`; `completeness7_run`; `alloc_owner_M_gap` |\n      | 5 | `runAmF_newMutex_authority`, `runAmF_protocol_authority` |\n      | 6 | `newMutexAm_effect`, `ctlGraph_init_write`, the corollaries |\n\n   4. Then the audit: 2462 = 2397 + 65, 1642 = 1592 + 50, 119 jobs, grep empty.\n   5. Last line, what is unchecked: the two-context W-NC, the WC4 `EncapsulatedTrace` traces under Run7, and the provider exclusion (posed, not exhibited).\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"b3d1c0b5-237b-4d0d-8791-b07764e7f182","timestamp":"2026-11-12T08:04:54.111Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":25,"turnIndex":32},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["9d895ccd-94b7-45e2-a639-7d588736a9d0"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
