h","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"3aaba682-f297-47fc-a8d5-aaa6d7e8791c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"048ce1b3-8891-4aae-bdd2-33b7fc094ee0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HQQX9Stdg14L4T9fMcbJAJ","type":"tool_result","content":"## C5. Provisional By-Value Transmission at `spawn`\n\nA `spawn` may provisionally transmit an owned value into a freshly created local destination in the new context. This is a **single composite candidate transition** with the following ordered phases, not an ordinary sequential execution of O6 followed by O4:\n\n1. **Create:** create the new context and initial frame, fresh local places, and their root authorities, **without yet yielding the access parameters**. This intermediate construction establishes destination places and their `Uninit` leaves, while the creator remains the executing frame for source checks.\n2. **Transfer:** transfer each by-value source into its designated fresh destination. All non-resulting-state O4 requirements, including source-side `Modify` exercise and the external-authority restriction of O4.4, are evaluated **at the start of the corresponding transfer phase**, after local construction but before any access parameter is yielded. For multiple by-value arguments, the candidate uses their explicit argument order and evaluates each against the state produced by earlier transfers. Source and destination footprints are disjoint and their ordered structural shapes match.\n3. **Yield:** at the beginning of this phase, in the state produced by the preceding value transfers, each transmitted authority must again satisfy the applicable parameter requirements of Spec 1 §72.1: it is active, derived, and held by the creator frame. Yield the declared access parameters to the child initial frame without duplication. Requirements that apply before the composite remain independently required.\n4. **Final checks:** evaluate O4's expressly resulting-state conditions (including §§63.6–63.9 as applicable), O6.3 and O6.4, and the applicable anchor and parameter-passing conditions on the final state. Preserve the correspondence of all effects to O4 and O6.\n\n**Additional candidate preconditions**\n\n1. The creator has exercisable `Modify` over every source's relevant footprint at its transfer phase; the source is usable and its required leaves are `Init`.\n2. Every destination is a fresh local root of the child, with corresponding `Uninit` leaves, no derived authorities and a `Modify` root authority held by the child frame under `RootHeld`.\n3. Only O4.1's **ordinary destination-side exercisability requirement** is replaced by the special fresh-destination construction condition. The source-side exercise condition remains required.\n4. Every other applicable precondition of O4 remains required, including pinning, validity, external-derived-authority restrictions, self-blocking prevention, and final destination usability.\n5. **No access parameter to be yielded may cover any leaf of any by-value source transferred by the same composite.** The test uses the declared source footprints before consumption, preventing a parameter from remaining associated with leaves becoming `Moved`.\n6. No exclusive authority, dependent right or owned resource is duplicated by the composite.\n\n**Effects**\n\nThe transfer phase marks consumed source leaves `Moved`, corresponding destination leaves `Init`, and relocates the corresponding held authorities, ownership links and dependencies by O4's effects. The yield phase changes holders of the access parameters and creates no rights.\n\n**Preservation obligations, not additional preconditions:** The final transition must preserve `ConcurrentWF`, I1–I4, the applicable anchor ordering properties, `NoDangling` and `NoOrphan`. These must be established by proofs of the composite, not inserted as assumed final-state conjuncts.\n\n**Outcome:** `ok` or `reject`.\n\nThis is an experimental calling convention for Spec 2, not a finalized rule for Spec 3. The exact proof obligations remain open under `OB-C09` and `OB-C14`.\n\n## C6. Frame Exit and Reparenting\n------\n## C13. Reference Construction — `newMutex`\n\n`newMutex` is a library operation establishing a synchronized authority-administration entry. Let `slot` be the place holding `guarded`, `M` its immediate structural parent and `ctl = ControlOf(M,slot)` its controller leaf.\n\n**Preconditions**\n\n1. `guarded` is active, of own mode `Modify`, and legally held by the usable `slot`.\n2. The constructing frame has ordinary exercisable `Modify` over `guarded` under Spec 1 §43.\n3. The declared structural positions identify the usable `slot` and a usable controller **leaf** `ctl` in the same `M`.\n4. `footprint(guarded) ∩ footprint(M) = ∅`. This is the reference mutex's structural disjointness requirement, allowing the control value `M` to be shared under compatible `Observe` authorities while `guarded` exclusively protects a distinct storage footprint.\n5. If `guarded` is stored by O8, the construction respects O8.3. In the reference arrangement, the protected root `T` is owned by `M`, not by `slot`; its leaves are not thereby included in `footprint(M)`.\n6. `K.SharedMutable(ctl)` holds for the controller leaf.\n7. The `guarded` identity is not registered as a live administrative identity by any other registered administration. This is an unconditional candidate unified consistency guard, following the non-duplication principle of Spec 1 §56.\n8. **Controller uniqueness:** no other live synchronization entry is associated with `ctl`. The association is injective among live entries.\n9. No active descendant of `guarded` covers a leaf of `footprint(guarded)`.\n10. **Initialization:** all structural leaves in `footprint(M)` are `Init` before construction. The operation does not implicitly initialize them. Storage merely owned by `M`, but structurally outside `footprint(M)`, is not included in this requirement solely by ownership.\n11. **Controller-initialization authority [WC5.2]:** The constructing frame has ordinary exercisable `Modify` authority with effective mode `Modify` over the controller leaf `ctl`, under Spec 1 §43 and the applicable ordinary-write requirements of O10.1 (§67.1). The ordinary-write exclusivity requirement of O10.2 (Spec 1 §67.2) also applies to this non-atomic write; its derivation from the reachable-state invariants is not separately established by the cited Lean checks. This authority is required to justify the non-atomic physical write establishing the controller's initial available state. A controller-access right sufficient only for an `Observe`-mode shared mutation under Spec 1 §68.2 does not satisfy this requirement.\n\n**Effect**\n\nThe library registers an initially available `SyncEntry { guarded, grant = none }`, without creating another access authority over the protected storage or initializing any leaf of `M`. Library administration state remains separate from `S_C`.\n\n**Controller-initialization clarification [WC5.2]:** This is an abstract registration effect: the operation changes no structural leaf's abstract initialization state. C13.10 already requires every structural leaf of `M`, including `ctl`, to be `Init` before construction; `newMutex` does not change an `Uninit` leaf to `Init`. Separately, the physical realization establishes the controller's initial available synchronization value by a **non-atomic write** to `ctl`, justified by C13.11 and subject to the applicable O10.1/O10.2 requirements. The term *controller initialization* in C31 and C48 denotes that physical synchronization-state write, not a transition of abstract structural initialization state. The non-atomic write is represented as an initial modification in `mo` under C31; it does not itself establish `sw`. Its concrete event, the ordering of this write with accesses in other execution contexts, and the correspondence with the initially available registry entry remain obligations under C27–C29, C42, C48 and `OB-C05`. The authority-only kernel state `S_C` does not establish the physical write or its ordering.\n\n**Preservation obligation:** The construction must establish the entire `SyncInv` and `GrantDiscipline` suite for the new and previously live entries. This is not an additional resulting-state precondition.\n\n**Interface and realization obligations:** The safe public interface must prevent falsification of the positional controller association (C13.3); the controller synchronization protocol (C13.6) must be enforced; and the initial physical controller state must correspond to the newly available abstract registry entry. C13.11 supplies a required authority premise for the initial ordinary write, but does not by itself prove its ordering with other contexts or its target realization. These are not claimed to follow from the authority-only state `S_C`. **[WC5.2 — exploratory evidence]** W-NC demonstrates that C13.1–C13.10 alone admit construction without controller rights; the added C13.11 rejects it in the amended model, while all 16 previously recorded construction steps satisfy the new premise. The abstract `newMutex` effect is unchanged.\n\nA reference representation may place the protected value in a distinct logical owned-storage root. No separate physical allocation is implied.\n\n## C14. Concurrent External Contract — `SyncAuthorized`\n\n`K_C` extends the unchanged Spec 1 contract `K`. The proposed concurrent authorization predicate accepts the **current logical synchronization registry as an explicit external argument**:\n\n```\nK_C.SyncAuthorized(state, sync_registry, guarded, requesting_frame)\n```\n\nThe registry is supplied by the library contract and is not part of the kernel state `S_C`. It must refer to the same logical registry state used for the candidate library transition.\n\nFor the reference mutex, the library's **authorization facts**, and only these facts, are:\n\n1. There exists a live registered entry with the requested `guarded` identity.\n2. That entry has `grant = none`.\n3. The requesting frame has the required effective and exercisable access to `ControlOf(entry)` under the controller-access obligation corresponding to Spec 1 §68.2.\n\nThe library must prove, under `ConcurrentWF`, the applicable Spec 1 invariants, `SyncInv`, `GrantDiscipline`, and the abstraction's encapsulation contract, that these facts imply the remaining authority prerequisites for `deriveSync`, including origin-chain validity, sufficient effective mode, absence of blocking descendants and I1 conservation.\n\nThe opaque authorization predicate must not be defined by simply conjoining the conclusions the library is required to prove. Its instantiation is state-dependent, and correctness must be reestablished for every enabled acquisition.\n\n`SyncAuthorized` does not create an authority, does not introduce ambient context rights, and cannot be used outside the corresponding valid synchronization contract. The precise synchronized physical realization remains deferred under `OB-C05`.\n\n## C15. New Concurrent Transition — `deriveSync`\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5ed9d2b4-4b2b-478d-9baa-fdc1eaa196c3","timestamp":"2026-11-12T16:25:35.984Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## C5. Provisional By-Value Transmission at `spawn`\n\nA `spawn` may provisionally transmit an owned value into a freshly created local destination in the new context. This is a **single composite candidate transition** with the following ordered phases, not an ordinary sequential execution of O6 followed by O4:\n\n1. **Create:** create the new context and initial frame, fresh local places, and their root authorities, **without yet yielding the access parameters**. This intermediate construction establishes destination places and their `Uninit` leaves, while the creator remains the executing frame for source checks.\n2. **Transfer:** transfer each by-value source into its designated fresh destination. All non-resulting-state O4 requirements, including source-side `Modify` exercise and the external-authority restriction of O4.4, are evaluated **at the start of the corresponding transfer phase**, after local construction but before any access parameter is yielded. For multiple by-value arguments, the candidate uses their explicit argument order and evaluates each against the state produced by earlier transfers. Source and destination footprints are disjoint and their ordered structural shapes match.\n3. **Yield:** at the beginning of this phase, in the state produced by the preceding value transfers, each transmitted authority must again satisfy the applicable parameter requirements of Spec 1 §72.1: it is active, derived, and held by the creator frame. Yield the declared access parameters to the child initial frame without duplication. Requirements that apply before the composite remain independently required.\n4. **Final checks:** evaluate O4's expressly resulting-state conditions (including §§63.6–63.9 as applicable), O6.3 and O6.4, and the applicable anchor and parameter-passing conditions on the final state. Preserve the correspondence of all effects to O4 and O6.\n\n**Additional candidate preconditions**\n\n1. The creator has exercisable `Modify` over every source's relevant footprint at its transfer phase; the source is usable and its required leaves are `Init`.\n2. Every destination is a fresh local root of the child, with corresponding `Uninit` leaves, no derived authorities and a `Modify` root authority held by the child frame under `RootHeld`.\n3. Only O4.1's **ordinary destination-side exercisability requirement** is replaced by the special fresh-destination construction condition. The source-side exercise condition remains required.\n4. Every other applicable precondition of O4 remains required, including pinning, validity, external-derived-authority restrictions, self-blocking prevention, and final destination usability.\n5. **No access parameter to be yielded may cover any leaf of any by-value source transferred by the same composite.** The test uses the declared source footprints before consumption, preventing a parameter from remaining associated with leaves becoming `Moved`.\n6. No exclusive authority, dependent right or owned resource is duplicated by the composite.\n\n**Effects**\n\nThe transfer phase marks consumed source leaves `Moved`, corresponding destination leaves `Init`, and relocates the corresponding held authorities, ownership links and dependencies by O4's effects. The yield phase changes holders of the access parameters and creates no rights.\n\n**Preservation obligations, not additional preconditions:** The final transition must preserve `ConcurrentWF`, I1–I4, the applicable anchor ordering properties, `NoDangling` and `NoOrphan`. These must be established by proofs of the composite, not inserted as assumed final-state conjuncts.\n\n**Outcome:** `ok` or `reject`.\n\nThis is an experimental calling convention for Spec 2, not a finalized rule for Spec 3. The exact proof obligations remain open under `OB-C09` and `OB-C14`.\n\n## C6. Frame Exit and Reparenting\n------\n## C13. Reference Construction — `newMutex`\n\n`newMutex` is a library operation establishing a synchronized authority-administration entry. Let `slot` be the place holding `guarded`, `M` its immediate structural parent and `ctl = ControlOf(M,slot)` its controller leaf.\n\n**Preconditions**\n\n1. `guarded` is active, of own mode `Modify`, and legally held by the usable `slot`.\n2. The constructing frame has ordinary exercisable `Modify` over `guarded` under Spec 1 §43.\n3. The declared structural positions identify the usable `slot` and a usable controller **leaf** `ctl` in the same `M`.\n4. `footprint(guarded) ∩ footprint(M) = ∅`. This is the reference mutex's structural disjointness requirement, allowing the control value `M` to be shared under compatible `Observe` authorities while `guarded` exclusively protects a distinct storage footprint.\n5. If `guarded` is stored by O8, the construction respects O8.3. In the reference arrangement, the protected root `T` is owned by `M`, not by `slot`; its leaves are not thereby included in `footprint(M)`.\n6. `K.SharedMutable(ctl)` holds for the controller leaf.\n7. The `guarded` identity is not registered as a live administrative identity by any other registered administration. This is an unconditional candidate unified consistency guard, following the non-duplication principle of Spec 1 §56.\n8. **Controller uniqueness:** no other live synchronization entry is associated with `ctl`. The association is injective among live entries.\n9. No active descendant of `guarded` covers a leaf of `footprint(guarded)`.\n10. **Initialization:** all structural leaves in `footprint(M)` are `Init` before construction. The operation does not implicitly initialize them. Storage merely owned by `M`, but structurally outside `footprint(M)`, is not included in this requirement solely by ownership.\n11. **Controller-initialization authority [WC5.2]:** The constructing frame has ordinary exercisable `Modify` authority with effective mode `Modify` over the controller leaf `ctl`, under Spec 1 §43 and the applicable ordinary-write requirements of O10.1 (§67.1). The ordinary-write exclusivity requirement of O10.2 (Spec 1 §67.2) also applies to this non-atomic write; its derivation from the reachable-state invariants is not separately established by the cited Lean checks. This authority is required to justify the non-atomic physical write establishing the controller's initial available state. A controller-access right sufficient only for an `Observe`-mode shared mutation under Spec 1 §68.2 does not satisfy this requirement.\n\n**Effect**\n\nThe library registers an initially available `SyncEntry { guarded, grant = none }`, without creating another access authority over the protected storage or initializing any leaf of `M`. Library administration state remains separate from `S_C`.\n\n**Controller-initialization clarification [WC5.2]:** This is an abstract registration effect: the operation changes no structural leaf's abstract initialization state. C13.10 already requires every structural leaf of `M`, including `ctl`, to be `Init` before construction; `newMutex` does not change an `Uninit` leaf to `Init`. Separately, the physical realization establishes the controller's initial available synchronization value by a **non-atomic write** to `ctl`, justified by C13.11 and subject to the applicable O10.1/O10.2 requirements. The term *controller initialization* in C31 and C48 denotes that physical synchronization-state write, not a transition of abstract structural initialization state. The non-atomic write is represented as an initial modification in `mo` under C31; it does not itself establish `sw`. Its concrete event, the ordering of this write with accesses in other execution contexts, and the correspondence with the initially available registry entry remain obligations under C27–C29, C42, C48 and `OB-C05`. The authority-only kernel state `S_C` does not establish the physical write or its ordering.\n\n**Preservation obligation:** The construction must establish the entire `SyncInv` and `GrantDiscipline` suite for the new and previously live entries. This is not an additional resulting-state precondition.\n\n**Interface and realization obligations:** The safe public interface must prevent falsification of the positional controller association (C13.3); the controller synchronization protocol (C13.6) must be enforced; and the initial physical controller state must correspond to the newly available abstract registry entry. C13.11 supplies a required authority premise for the initial ordinary write, but does not by itself prove its ordering with other contexts or its target realization. These are not claimed to follow from the authority-only state `S_C`. **[WC5.2 — exploratory evidence]** W-NC demonstrates that C13.1–C13.10 alone admit construction without controller rights; the added C13.11 rejects it in the amended model, while all 16 previously recorded construction steps satisfy the new premise. The abstract `newMutex` effect is unchanged.\n\nA reference representation may place the protected value in a distinct logical owned-storage root. No separate physical allocation is implied.\n\n## C14. Concurrent External Contract — `SyncAuthorized`\n\n`K_C` extends the unchanged Spec 1 contract `K`. The proposed concurrent authorization predicate accepts the **current logical synchronization registry as an explicit external argument**:\n\n```\nK_C.SyncAuthorized(state, sync_registry, guarded, requesting_frame)\n```\n\nThe registry is supplied by the library contract and is not part of the kernel state `S_C`. It must refer to the same logical registry state used for the candidate library transition.\n\nFor the reference mutex, the library's **authorization facts**, and only these facts, are:\n\n1. There exists a live registered entry with the requested `guarded` identity.\n2. That entry has `grant = none`.\n3. The requesting frame has the required effective and exercisable access to `ControlOf(entry)` under the controller-access obligation corresponding to Spec 1 §68.2.\n\nThe library must prove, under `ConcurrentWF`, the applicable Spec 1 invariants, `SyncInv`, `GrantDiscipline`, and the abstraction's encapsulation contract, that these facts imply the remaining authority prerequisites for `deriveSync`, including origin-chain validity, sufficient effective mode, absence of blocking descendants and I1 conservation.\n\nThe opaque authorization predicate must not be defined by simply conjoining the conclusions the library is required to prove. Its instantiation is state-dependent, and correctness must be reestablished for every enabled acquisition.\n\n`SyncAuthorized` does not create an authority, does not introduce ambient context rights, and cannot be used outside the corresponding valid synchronization contract. The precise synchronized physical realization remains deferred under `OB-C05`.\n\n## C15. New Concurrent Transition — `deriveSync`","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"358596d3-5390-466e-9f1f-3a6cc5f4041b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3aaba682-f297-47fc-a8d5-aaa6d7e8791c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
